{
  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3784",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with multiple potassium channel subunits, specifically Kcna3, Kcnd1, and Kcnc3, all of which are involved in the regulation of potassium channel activity. This binding is supported by high-confidence scores across three distinct paths, indicating a consistent and significant interaction. The shared involvement of these subunits in the \"Outward Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity\" and \"Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity\" suggests that Guanidine may modulate potassium channel function through a common mechanism. The presence of these activities in the context of Kcnq1, a known subunit of the delayed rectifier potassium channel, implies that Guanidine could influence the function of this channel, potentially affecting cellular potassium homeostasis. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Guanidine and Kcnq1, particularly through its impact on potassium channel activity, which is a critical aspect of cellular physiology.",
